 {:db/id "q-127737" :question/id #uuid "e9cf7ac8-28c7-510c-8205-256a03a04ef2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127737" :question/problem "Calculate ${U}^{-1}$, where \n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $U$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(U)=-2\\cdot 7-(-5)\\cdot 3=1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(U)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -(-5) & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U{U}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {U}^{-1}U & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127737/ma-source-field/4b455212074f8a6318f8f9676766203401985ad4af4d22496ec12e4706af70e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
