 {:db/id "q-128499" :question/id #uuid "0fce542a-476c-5ad1-ad5a-b30b8a4bb006" :question/math-academy-id "q-128499" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(1,5,13)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-7,12,5⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-9,21,2⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,4,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,5,-3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(1,5,13)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨1,5,13⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨1,5,13⟩+s⟨-2,4,1⟩+t⟨2,5,-3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-128499/ma-source-field/1a95d056b5f94964012324f767ff172767bc8df4eb544ab694ecff5b87c0e35e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
