 {:db/id "q-129480" :question/id #uuid "238922a6-1ae9-598b-83f3-1fd25fd1bf01" :question/math-academy-id "q-129480" :question/problem "What are the dimensions of $CD$, if $C$ is a $5\\times 7$ matrix and $D$ is a $7\\times 1$ matrix?" :question/worked-solution "There are $7$ columns in $C$ and $7$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $C$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication, and $CD$ is a $5\\times 1$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{C}_{5\\times \\boxed{\\text{7}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{7}}\\times 1}={CD}_{5\\times 1}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129480/ma-source-field/97e416c242c1ad261694a0d2ecc4cb409b33c27fd7a52280fe8b1c0e164791ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
