 {:db/id "q-134085" :question/id #uuid "6b5dde64-1d37-5f32-890c-5a590a1188e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134085" :question/problem "![](images/55/551ed1182231e19a08653c86ffb7b117c2dc9497b6927f6287ffcd10651b5f56.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the size of a class. How many absences were there in a class whose size is $20$ students?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/80/8088e41a66b4aba259d95f3099f71d5777caf876e9278e6b7f11c865ab12f7e0.png)\n\nTo determine the number of absences there were in a class whose size is $20$ students, we locate $20$ on the horizontal axis and move in the vertical direction until we find some points, as shown above.\n\nThe highlighted point has coordinates $(20,6).$ Therefore, there was a total of $6$ absences in the month for the class with $20$ students." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134085/ma-source-field/410c04f8b1c31fe53eb0a8a4b90b1cfbb7f3980a241fb3afeb3edbba3bb3682f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
