 {:db/id "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a5589d-c173-52b7-aa4e-ec8dcdd731a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/070f2b56dbe050630c4363adfc797fc58ea7428b344d273f031beabe7cd00a74" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/567a64af3d04fe8efb60cb1e6ffdee37abc4f4e013e17830ec47d7c2bd0134fe" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/a760d88544f9e6d6751fa895a91d61a1a3c62de45b6b6481bdacaad4229d6c1e" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/9100b1dbbb946d559fdc454853210252487344d1dcbac664210d0980ddad3817" "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/17fd5cccc0c009af443b9a90a37e700541651671791b5545778d8ce8f5399d75"] :answer-field/correct "q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc/a760d88544f9e6d6751fa895a91d61a1a3c62de45b6b6481bdacaad4229d6c1e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-135105" :question/id #uuid "04947b95-8a1f-567f-948f-2de5de86130e" :question/math-academy-id "q-135105" :question/problem "An object is projected vertically down from a height of $0.6\\,\\text{km}$ and hits the ground in $6\\,\\text{s}.$ What was the initial velocity of the object?\n\n*Hint: The acceleration due to gravity is $9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we use the formula\n\n$$\ns=ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the displacement, measured from the starting position in the direction of the initial motion, $u$ is the initial velocity, $t$ is the time since the beginning of the motion, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.\n\nLet's summarize the information we have:\n\n- The object falls for $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- We can find the distance the object falls in meters as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =0.6\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\text{km}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\cancel{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}} \\\\  & =0.6\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =600\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (600) & =u(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(6)^{2} \\\\ 600 & =6u+176.4 \\\\ 423.6 & =6u \\\\ u & =70.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the object was $u=70.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135105/ma-source-field/1416638441702675b198b17e58102ff48a77777a7314d64fa16b0f9bfc62b3cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
