 {:db/id "q-136311" :question/id #uuid "9d9adc28-1eef-586b-9169-6940ecdacba5" :question/math-academy-id "q-136311" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the speed of the particle, rounding your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|2i-5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\  & ≈5.39\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-136311/ma-source-field/3322ad499f30df09b5186f6fc3f02a17c5cacd56f7a828a15f2ed1cda9ddfcd2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
