 {:db/id "q-136312" :question/id #uuid "ede10ea1-892c-5590-9caf-f40ffde6984b" :question/math-academy-id "q-136312" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=(i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle, rounding your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|i+4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17} \\\\  & ≈4.12\\,\\text{km/h}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-136312/ma-source-field/8e524d4e98ccc82d18c9aee6123dabe32fce1606ac19a2c083d05d22a3c94298"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
