 {:db/id "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8654e2b-81b1-59db-ab37-3633e783690a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/a7f0a4abb777b92223acd7ca14e86c457c6fb6d17de30b11d59cef0f85d1f04d" "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/3be7ff7bd3ad5ccddd3743ec0bf3e4df801943871648b9ce68bb41915c280f03" "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/8ae659b6a953ab86b23c1fa441d47dd65b4f315cb0586462816b8c681a3ed3fa" "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/d4dfc1695ca035b3660f55595eb11bd770be7ab8fd2d99ddba98d0079ef6b681" "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/91cc8b641688b12da4bc3641c65b25740d28ee96c582e889097ba6a70af63730"] :answer-field/correct "q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877/d4dfc1695ca035b3660f55595eb11bd770be7ab8fd2d99ddba98d0079ef6b681" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-136355" :question/id #uuid "b1f34d54-8942-568b-886d-8135a1e4e0a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-136355" :question/problem "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+3j,\\,a=-i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ seconds, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-3i+6j) \\\\  & =(2i+9j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|2i+9j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85} \\\\  & ≈9.22\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-136355/ma-source-field/03200a404f1e027b6b69c82210fa4a80b50c34f0b83bb834a6520b505231b877"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
