 {:db/id "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408" :answer-field/id #uuid "25043d55-6e38-5a47-9ce8-35564e623dc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :answer-field/correct "q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-142000" :question/id #uuid "949bd398-6573-53d2-bf2d-21cf0dde3f19" :question/math-academy-id "q-142000" :question/problem "![](images/98/98edb404419e7ab515109f87addb44709513007b1a0105b648a3ce2b62ad547f.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+1=4.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142000/ma-source-field/e004de41ebe268520fd770b1ba530c38f05579b5f53f54d5fb7a1d0b787ca408"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
