 {:db/id "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a33bc7f4-158e-59b4-b555-27008daa9757" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/671723d87f1a67d9aa6a1f954b934e271d81eedfb75a65037fca3403ebebfd96" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :answer-field/correct "q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-143669" :question/id #uuid "d39218d1-1972-5152-bee8-516235be3a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-143669" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f86984919b15283134e1b3a9479ff8c79ec8dfacc84975e82f88704b7b26dd3a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is  $B-2D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=4.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{9}{4}$ unit down. Therefore, $D=-\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, $B-2D=4-2\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{4})=4+\\frac{9}{2}=\\frac{17}{2}.$  \n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143669/ma-source-field/20b70f06716ddbb3889b157af4779928962aa640544eeb1b2ab508b5710eb60a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
