 {:db/id "q-149766" :question/id #uuid "5df16893-ba76-5e94-9eac-1e75b05b6b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149766" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=X+3.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $b$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $c$ | $d$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=X+3$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=-3,b=5,c=0.1,$ and therefore $a+b+c=2.1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149766/ma-source-field/b616f07b8bb2f51a5122f18013ea2d3f445a374797d1f0805f2f59536458ac28"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
