 {:db/id "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f44abc-ac48-5c5f-840d-7b78fa1a5463" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/821dd8ed7daef7398474de64a02ed06acb0ff0876b3c43c33c7514bed5d0390b" "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/628ce67488c1409828dd68ac0270d9a964bc03018b0663c2af65f2ad092760a1" "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/846df385986ecd89ffcf1c04d1cb44f6fa18b34ef014428437ad80af48635d31" "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/6f90d1d1d67d59368a2daea8e4e7c86d4e84eae5963dd53759dd92c5283187bf" "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/189c768f44ab7aa866abd1b7ebb5ab93712265b7dc1fa61cf8d9ee7cd70248d8"] :answer-field/correct "q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b/846df385986ecd89ffcf1c04d1cb44f6fa18b34ef014428437ad80af48635d31" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161086" :question/id #uuid "e82a0cbf-06e5-5031-a4c7-160ebc24fbd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161086" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n\n$$\ny=2x,\\,y=5x,\\,y=\\frac{3}{x},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x}.\n$$\n\nA transformation $T,$ where\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nmaps a rectangular region $Δ$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\,,\\,\\,\\sqrt{uv}),\n$$\n\nwhat could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\ny=2x,\\,y=5x,\\,y=\\frac{3}{x},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x}=2,\\,\\frac{y}{x}=5,\\,xy=3,\\,xy=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ and $v(x,y)=xy,$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{y}{x}\\,,\\,xy).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ v=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $y=ux.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $y=ux,$ we obtain\n\n$$\ny=u\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt{uv}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{v}{u}},\\,\\sqrt{uv}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161086/ma-source-field/7d16f54998fd1be8a76bd1219650d8760bc74d45494e30dda60685bb3da5438b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
