 {:db/id "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f48bed04-e645-581d-90b2-d43b8caed324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/b0ad8c6d527eb7879c4db50f366aaa11ab38bf63a6600430da769cb6f7e2bfe8" "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/a564df14b9f3fd4776b074f9ffb8a0d598600f9ea76de4e05ad223355200e9cb" "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/7c09c2380253f3967cc094968b27fb927489ccbbecd250a4ae799721371f3b6d" "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/07f604a1a5724ff73ed3947f1895e0cd15f32c1031456f0e01983df159dad57c" "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/62a3fa3bcf27f412ebd28dc07ab53529ee00902b164351c9b1c9c7098a3db42a"] :answer-field/correct "q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b/a564df14b9f3fd4776b074f9ffb8a0d598600f9ea76de4e05ad223355200e9cb" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161251" :question/id #uuid "50f21d4c-115f-5f6b-a6fe-50fa77f7169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161251" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)+3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)+{u}^{2}\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡v+{sin}^{2}⁡v)+{u}^{3} \\\\  & =-5{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,-5{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161251/ma-source-field/21fe55bd1569f729ff52cd789e789549880c9776ddb270c955940ce15a6c320b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
