 {:db/id "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30" :answer-field/id #uuid "d15555d0-ef8f-523d-8686-3e2c75b76cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/3483a8b73bef95f967c3ea109c98bfe9d90a6bbf466824ffab52b308a887400a" "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/95e55e09c8fd088b369b94477d725ae2e75cac1e692891f1ba56c531a79712c4" "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/6e59713f6b879702b491b97312323568e2b8ba7e2b05cbe3c2cdd120cb8436fd" "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/e1ba13e972f703b9c92836ec51aa344b6aa57627d23a0d26323d3f3acbe15d3e" "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/b457ef847266cf0f37ae72a63d53032673dd9a313030dd351d996287f2cfe925"] :answer-field/correct "q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30/e1ba13e972f703b9c92836ec51aa344b6aa57627d23a0d26323d3f3acbe15d3e" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161357" :question/id #uuid "eec4b66c-4af6-5b13-942b-337cb7b8732a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161357" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161357/ma-source-field/6f461694d6b705fbc23495e3cc068406619cc995ee475d84809ae4b132803e30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
