 {:db/id "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "396da9a4-de3b-5bd7-8b5e-dfc780e10bb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/c3d20475246818166b7bd614ae7dc243ccd19389acb8115a1367398a47870d0d" "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/da772ca5bbe7da853d2e6a3756f6ee2df1b44d18f238029ee5ac1fbea666e3c2" "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/eaae3272142bda04bf332ba57a7cee56c8de50819ed615ab69dfe74979a7eb07" "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/7159a960144a256245bf8387c88bea2e4b5e1b1ff6bb2a0b76dd9d85aee7518b" "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/c193e136e97cc4b0206137d7bc339daf600e96eec10a71c0cea8f06e3982d36b"] :answer-field/correct "q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b/7159a960144a256245bf8387c88bea2e4b5e1b1ff6bb2a0b76dd9d85aee7518b" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161359" :question/id #uuid "d5e1155b-c484-5f31-a815-946d2d63d6df" :question/math-academy-id "q-161359" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨(u-v)v,\\,(u-v)u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)v\\cdot (-1)+(u-v)u\\cdot (1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-uv+{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}-uv+uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨zy,\\,xz,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161359/ma-source-field/3240769f6bcec23f0fa71cbdd81880d8b0a9f9e80471eeaf348972ebc0b09b7b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
