 {:db/id "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "185487e5-090f-5815-93b2-dfc0c983e691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/d4dfee1d713efc201fde7860abe8dac58b5127f931b3cd399af5c017fa4e63f1" "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/b1c1b65814368dff35eac0b0e5912f2bd18c24d566e52278d206a5d2bbab9fbd" "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/aef05162c6e1334d7c7f14de08c6a85222303b11d7c1c4fa480d78bd14c1a549" "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/6298f8f959e14dd05a6923c80ed5003a42cb2ad6f758f2894c7767847a920c56" "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/c193e136e97cc4b0206137d7bc339daf600e96eec10a71c0cea8f06e3982d36b"] :answer-field/correct "q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf/b1c1b65814368dff35eac0b0e5912f2bd18c24d566e52278d206a5d2bbab9fbd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "a3bcb9d3-050c-5ab9-bd2a-436465223147"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}+2uv+{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161360/ma-source-field/cbd4105f4110afffd848078685078793a1c61f8c4750ad85df2ef1865308a1cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
