 {:db/id "q-161550" :question/id #uuid "a8f9ff3a-79fc-5066-8340-3c87867ab323" :question/math-academy-id "q-161550" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3ded2a039746e3c8f7a7ee4afb70b0d697468d1aee8f0e9dab24b1ca87897d2.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1946cea37f202705e6517ba760afa6617075f748901b10588ea98628a3e9e50.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola $2y={x}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2y={x}^{2}\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161550/ma-source-field/f92628938c22c42e12fa744a3b9d8a32ea6afef265fd70e56bc06272c1758f07"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
