 {:db/id "q-161598" :question/id #uuid "bcfdd46f-14ab-5535-a276-fcd0db509adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161598" :question/problem "![](images/11/112ab676fa5a97db198a872c33579900deab76e0c3c9c92016e165a67482bbcd.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/44/44f3a2a8e535c7248dac49d126da9bf17fce94c357f15c93a3eaad665e73b47a.png)\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36.$  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=36\\,}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-161598/ma-source-field/feaf7e758d9f1eb20bc5d75a4f090f4c63b8b76251abb9d0b81c094dcd409f65"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
