 {:db/id "q-162644" :question/id #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162644" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162644/ma-source-field/6ea465203304b33e29ea21ba9b69c62f89ca610a4d2a4f9cf7e36cb0f774c3dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
