 {:db/id "q-164249" :question/id #uuid "16dea1c4-5f05-52d5-8897-db965a563c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164249" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z & =12 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}-4z+4) & =12+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}={4}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164249/ma-source-field/dc960a14ed09c1214ef941ee7f398c7b05bb4639b061ddfd2c4c857100bb5592"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
