 {:db/id "q-164412" :question/id #uuid "75aa15a4-a235-5132-bf56-78143897ca7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164412" :question/problem "The projection of the intersection between the parabolic cylinder $3(x+2)^{2}=6(y+3)$ and the plane $z=4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a parabola. What is the vertex of the parabola?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $z=4,$ we substitute $z=4$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $z$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+2)^{2} & =6(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =2(y+3) \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (y+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a parabola in the $xy$-plane with the vertex at $(-2,-3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164412/ma-source-field/ba1c35976b4916b8a1300e91e194357dbb696ab53937cb8c24ca2b6bb1b7652e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
